ays declared that it wanted to  integrate economically with europe  and that's why it was seeking membership  with the european union  and  transnistria was seeking alignment  with russia  alignments made clearer on thursday when  moldova and georgia followed ukraine's  footsteps and applied to join the  european union a process in the making  for years that fast-tracked in just a  matter of days  al jazeera  anthony lincoln's also saying the us may  send planes to poland to backfill  warsaw's numbers if the polish  government sends some of its own planes  to help ukraine  we are  we're looking actively now  at the question of airplanes that poland  may provide to uh to ukraine and looking  at how we might be able to backfill  should poland decide to produce those to  supply those planes  can't speak to a timeline but i can just  tell you we're looking at it very very  actively  russia has warned countries against  hosting ukrainian military aircraft the  defense military says they'd be regarded  as being involved in the conflict  earlier president vladimir putin says  the invasion will only be halted if  ukraine stops what he calls its  hostilities he's blamed the kiev  government for the fighting  frank ludwig is a senior lecturer in  military capabilities and strategy at  the university of portsmouth he's also a  former military officer who served in  the balkans in iraq and afghanistan he  says the russian campaign in ukraine  appears to be lacking in preparation and  planning  well i think most analysts people like  myself take the view that the ukrainians  are coming up to prove  we expected them to be effective they've  been ready for this for years they've  been trained by western forces and if  you look at the way their regular forces  look the way they present themselves  they present themselves very much like  nato forces like british america french  or german troops professional  well-equipped and so forth  what's really shocking though is the way  the r